      "title": "Optimise the requested magnitude",
      "body": "<p>Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo></mrow></math>. For each interval you derived, compare the absolute values of its endpoints. Then check whether the two choices can occur together.</p>",
      "recap": "Independent interval constraints allow compatible endpoint choices, but the quantity to maximise is the magnitude.",
