  "solution": "<p>The bounds give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02208;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x02208;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x000B7;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>The pair x=8,y=−6 is allowed and attains 48. <strong>Answer E.</strong></p>",
